<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pinnes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 6–8 CE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pinnes was a Pannonian leader who took part with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bato-the-breucian">Bato the Breucian</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-illyrian-revolt">Great Illyrian Revolt</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> from 6 CE. In 8 CE Bato the Breucian handed him over to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> in return for favourable terms, a betrayal for which Bato was then executed by his ally <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bato-the-daesitiate">Bato the Daesitiate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pinnes.jpg" alt="Pinnes" width="320" height="309" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nishjan · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdom_of_the_Ardiaei,_late_3rd_century_B.C.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
